    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">margărītārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		margarita, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to pearls,
				pearl-</i> (postclass.): porticus, <i>where pearls
				were bought</i>, Auct. de Region. Urb. Rom. Reg.
			8.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">margărītārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a dealer in
				pearls, a pearl-fisher</i>, Firm. Math. 4, 6;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1602</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">4076</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4218</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Margărītārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a female
				dealer in pearls</i>, Inscr Orell. 4148.</div>
